.TH ARANET4\-GO 1 "2026-09-09" "aranet4-go" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aranet4\-go \- read CO2 and environmental data from an Aranet4 sensor via Bluetooth
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aranet4\-go
.B \-mac
.I ADDRESS
.RB [ \-json ]
.RB [ \-debug ]
.RB [ \-m ]
.br
.B aranet4\-go
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aranet4\-go
connects to an Aranet4 CO2 sensor over Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) and
prints the current CO2, temperature, humidity, pressure, battery level,
and air quality status.
.PP
The sensor must have
.B Smart Home Integration
enabled in the Aranet4 mobile app (firmware v1.2.0 or newer required).
No pairing or cloud connection is needed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-mac " ADDRESS"
Bluetooth MAC address of the Aranet4 sensor (e.g.\&
.IR FC:5C:65:B7:84:94 ).
Dashes are accepted in place of colons.
Required unless the binary was built with a hardcoded default address.
.TP
.B \-json
Print output as a JSON object instead of human-readable text.
.TP
.B \-debug
Print verbose diagnostic output to stderr: BLE scan progress, discovered
services and characteristics, and connection state.
.TP
.B \-m
Disable ANSI color coding.
Useful when piping output to a file or a tool that does not interpret
escape codes.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-version
Print the version, git commit, and build timestamp, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
.SS Human-readable (default)
.nf
CO2:         940 ppm
Temperature: 22.9 \[de]C
Humidity:    30 %
Pressure:    1013.7 hPa
Battery:     94 %
Status:      GREEN
Interval:    300 s
Age:         4m 23s
.fi
.PP
.B Interval
is the measurement period configured on the device.
.B Age
is the time elapsed since the last measurement was taken.
Values are color-coded green, yellow, or red according to the thresholds
described in
.B COLOR CODING
below.
Use
.B \-m
to disable colors.
.SS JSON
.nf
{
  "co2": 940,
  "temperature": 22.9,
  "pressure": 1013.7,
  "humidity": 30,
  "battery": 94,
  "status": "GREEN",
  "status_code": 1,
  "interval": 300,
  "ago": 263
}
.fi
.PP
.B ago
is in seconds.
.B status_code
is 1\~(GREEN), 2\~(YELLOW), or 3\~(RED) as reported by the device.
.SH COLOR CODING
.SS CO2 (ppm)
.TP
GREEN
< 1000 \(em good air quality
.TP
YELLOW
1000\(en1400 \(em consider ventilation
.TP
RED
> 1400 \(em ventilation needed
.SS Temperature (\[de]C)
.TP
GREEN
18\(en24
.TP
YELLOW
15\(en18 or 24\(en27
.TP
RED
< 15 or > 27
.SS Humidity (%)
.TP
GREEN
30\(en45
.TP
YELLOW
46\(en70
.TP
RED
< 30 or > 70
.SS Pressure (hPa)
.TP
GREEN
993\(en1033
.TP
YELLOW
980\(en992 or 1034\(en1050
.TP
RED
< 980 or > 1050
.SS Battery (%)
.TP
GREEN
> 30
.TP
YELLOW
15\(en30
.TP
RED
< 15
.PP
The overall
.B Status
field reflects the worst of the CO2 and humidity readings.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error: missing required flag, invalid MAC address, device not found,
BLE read failure, or invalid data received.
.SH EXAMPLES
Read from a specific device:
.PP
.RS
.nf
aranet4\-go \-mac FC:5C:65:B7:84:94
.fi
.RE
.PP
Emit JSON for scripting:
.PP
.RS
.nf
aranet4\-go \-mac FC:5C:65:B7:84:94 \-json | jq .co2
.fi
.RE
.PP
Log every five minutes via cron:
.PP
.RS
.nf
*/5 * * * * aranet4\-go \-mac FC:5C:65:B7:84:94 \-json >> /var/log/aranet4.log
.fi
.RE
.PP
Disable colors when piping:
.PP
.RS
.nf
aranet4\-go \-mac FC:5C:65:B7:84:94 \-m | tee readings.txt
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I DEFAULT\-MAC\-ADDR
If this file exists in the build directory, its contents are baked into
the binary as the default MAC address at compile time.
.SH NOTES
.SS Linux Bluetooth permissions
Raw Bluetooth access requires elevated privileges.
The recommended approach is to grant the binary the necessary capabilities
once after installation:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo setcap 'cap_net_raw,cap_net_admin=eip' /usr/local/bin/aranet4\-go
.fi
.RE
.PP
Alternatively, run with
.BR sudo (8)
or add your user to the
.B bluetooth
group.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR hcitool (1),
.BR jq (1)
.PP
Aranet4 Python library:
.I https://github.com/Anrijs/Aranet4-Python
